	(footprint "castle:D_SOD-123"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "60b19d1e-3473-4dac-bdac-117e7e6ab1fd")
		(at 99 63.5)
		(descr "SOD-123 - THREE parts share this land since v5: D5, the 12 V gate-clamp zener (MMSZ5242B-7-F), and D6/D7, the B5819W Schottkys that OR VBUS and the barrel into VBUCK. Pad 1 is the cathode, the banded end, and the silk prints the band beside it - so on D6 and D7 pad 1 is VBUCK and pad 2 is the source. A SOD-123 fitted 180 degrees out is a dead OR-ing diode, which is why they are on the placement-viewer list.")
