	(footprint "castle:ESP32-S3-WROOM-1"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "93710bb6-f8a1-4600-a2c2-32f45ebece1e")
		(at 118 53)
		(descr "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1, LCC-41, 18.0 x 25.5 x 3.1 mm - U2, the module this carrier is built around (Espressif datasheet v1.8, Table 3-1 and Figure 10-1). Pads 1-40 on a 1.27 mm pitch, pad 41 the EPAD as one land plus twelve plated thermal vias RE-DRILLED 0.30 mm on 0.80 mm lands (KiCad's stock 0.20/0.60 is under this project's own 0.30 mm hole floor and inside JLCPCB's small-hole surcharge - PAD_GEOM), and nine paste-only apertures that split the EPAD's stencil window (datasheet p.41: too much paste lifts the module off its other forty pads). Carries the antenna keep-out as a rule area on every copper layer. THE COURTYARD IS NOT THE STOCK ONE: it is the module body, because KiCad draws the keep-out as the courtyard too. It is the module body, 19.5 x 26.4 mm - docs/V5-SPEC.md sec 3.2.")
		(tags "2.4 GHz Wi-Fi and Bluetooth module")
